{"id":"mahabharata-5-093","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":93,"title":"त्रिनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 93 · Krishna's appeal in the assembly","summary":{"en":"Krishna addresses Dhritarashtra, urging him to make peace between the Kurus and Pandavas, which lies in his power alone, and warning that war will destroy the earth's kings. He reminds him of the Pandavas' patience and loyalty and asks him to restore their share and live as their father; the kings silently applaud.","kn":"ಕುರು ಪಾಂಡವರ ನಡುವೆ ಶಾಂತಿ ಸ್ಥಾಪಿಸುವುದು ನಿನ್ನ ಕೈಯಲ್ಲೇ ಇದೆ, ಯುದ್ಧ ಭೂಮಿಯ ರಾಜರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡುವುದು ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನನ್ನು ಉದ್ದೇಶಿಸಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪಾಂಡವರ ತಾಳ್ಮೆ ನಿಷ್ಠೆಗಳನ್ನು ನೆನಪಿಸಿ ಅವರ ಪಾಲನ್ನು ಮರಳಿಸಿ ತಂದೆಯಂತೆ ಬಾಳು ಎಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾಜರು ಮೌನವಾಗಿ ಮೆಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण धृतराष्ट्र को सम्बोधित कर कुरुओं और पाण्डवों के बीच शान्ति स्थापित करने का आग्रह करते हैं, जो केवल उनके हाथ में है, और चेताते हैं कि युद्ध पृथ्वी के राजाओं का नाश कर देगा। वे पाण्डवों के धैर्य और निष्ठा की याद दिलाकर उनका भाग लौटाने और उनके पिता की तरह रहने को कहते हैं; राजा मौन होकर सराहना करते हैं।","te":"కురు పాండవుల మధ్య శాంతి నెలకొల్పడం నీ చేతిలోనే ఉందని, యుద్ధం భూమిపై రాజులను నాశనం చేస్తుందని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు ధృతరాష్ట్రుని ఉద్దేశించి చెబుతాడు. పాండవుల ఓర్పు, నిష్ఠలను గుర్తుచేసి వారి వాటాను తిరిగి ఇచ్చి తండ్రిలా జీవించమని కోరతాడు; రాజులు మౌనంగా మెచ్చుకుంటారు.","ta":"குருக்களுக்கும் பாண்டவர்களுக்கும் இடையே அமைதியை நிலைநாட்டுவது உம் கையில் மட்டுமே உள்ளது, போர் பூமியின் மன்னர்களை அழிக்கும் என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் த்ருதராஷ்டிரனை நோக்கிச் சொல்கிறார். பாண்டவர்களின் பொறுமையையும் பற்றையும் நினைவூட்டி, அவர்கள் பங்கைத் திருப்பித் தந்து அவர்களுக்குத் தந்தையாக வாழுமாறு கேட்க, மன்னர்கள் மௌனமாகப் பாராட்டுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"കുരുക്കളും പാണ്ഡവരും തമ്മിൽ സമാധാനമുണ്ടാക്കുന്നത് തന്റെ മാത്രം കൈയിലാണെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരെ അഭിസംബോധന ചെയ്ത് കൃഷ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു; യുദ്ധം ഭൂമിയിലെ രാജാക്കന്മാരെ നശിപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവരുടെ ക്ഷമയും വിശ്വസ്തതയും ഓർമ്മിപ്പിച്ച്, അവരുടെ പങ്ക് തിരികെ നൽകി പിതാവിനെപ്പോലെ ജീവിക്കാൻ അദ്ദേഹം അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; രാജാക്കന്മാർ മൗനമായി അംഗീകരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.93; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तेष्वासीनेषु सर्वेषु तूष्णींभूतेषु राजसु ।\nवाक्यमभ्याददे कृष्णः सुदंष्ट्रो दुन्दुभिस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all were seated and the kings were silent, Krishna, with fine teeth and a voice like a kettledrum, began to speak."}},{"n":2,"text":"जीमूत इव घर्मान्ते सर्वां संश्रावयन्सभाम् ।\nधृतराष्ट्रमभिप्रेक्ष्य समभाषत माधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a rain cloud at summer's end, making the whole assembly hear, Madhava looked at Dhritarashtra and said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"कुरूणां पाण्डवानां च शमः स्यादिति भारत ।\nअप्रयत्नेन वीराणामेतद्यतितुमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, I have come so that peace may be made between Kurus and Pandavas without the slaughter of heroes."}},{"n":4,"text":"राजन्नान्यत्प्रवक्तव्यं तव निःश्रेयसं वचः ।\nविदितं ह्येव ते सर्वं वेदितव्यमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I have no other beneficial thing to tell you; for you already know everything that is to be known, subduer of foes."}},{"n":5,"text":"इदमद्य कुलं श्रेष्ठं सर्वराजसु पार्थिव ।\nश्रुतवृत्तोपसंपन्नं सर्वैः समुदितं गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This family today is the foremost among all kings, endowed with learning and conduct and every virtue."}},{"n":6,"text":"कृपानुकम्पा कारुण्यमानृशंस्यं च भारत ।\nतथार्जवं क्षमा सत्यं कुरुष्वेतद्विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the Kurus, Bharata, compassion, kindness, pity, gentleness, uprightness, forgiveness and truth are especially prized."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्मिन्नेवंविधे राजन्कुले महति तिष्ठति ।\nत्वन्निमित्तं विशेषेण नेह युक्तमसांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, when such a great family exists, it is especially unfitting and wrong, on your account, that anything improper should happen here."}},{"n":8,"text":"त्वं हि वारयिता श्रेष्ठः कुरूणां कुरुसत्तम ।\nमिथ्या प्रचरतां तात बाह्येष्वाभ्यन्तरेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of Kurus, you are the chief one who should restrain the Kurus who behave falsely toward outsiders and within."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते पुत्रास्तव कौरव्य दुर्योधनपुरोगमाः ।\nधर्मार्थौ पृष्ठतः कृत्वा प्रचरन्ति नृशंसवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kaurava, those sons of yours, led by Duryodhana, behave cruelly, putting dharma and profit behind them."}},{"n":10,"text":"अशिष्टा गतमर्यादा लोभेन हृतचेतसः ।\nस्वेषु बन्धुषु मुख्येषु तद्वेत्थ भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, you know that, being ill-mannered, beyond limits and robbed of judgment by greed, they act so toward their own chief kinsmen."}},{"n":11,"text":"सेयमापन्महाघोरा कुरुष्वेव समुत्थिता ।\nउपेक्ष्यमाणा कौरव्य पृथिवीं घातयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"This most terrible calamity has arisen among the Kurus; if neglected, Kaurava, it will destroy the earth."}},{"n":12,"text":"शक्या चेयं शमयितुं त्वं चेदिच्छसि भारत ।\nन दुष्करो ह्यत्र शमो मतो मे भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"It can be quieted, Bharata, if you wish; in my view peace here is not hard to make."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्वय्यधीनः शमो राजन्मयि चैव विशां पते ।\nपुत्रान्स्थापय कौरव्य स्थापयिष्याम्यहं परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Peace depends on you, king, and on me. Set your sons right, Kaurava, and I shall set the other side right."}},{"n":14,"text":"आज्ञा तव हि राजेन्द्र कार्या पुत्रैः सहान्वयैः ।\nहितं बलवदप्येषां तिष्ठतां तव शासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your command should be obeyed by your sons and their followers; it would be best for them to remain under your rule."}},{"n":15,"text":"तव चैव हितं राजन्पाण्डवानामथो हितम् ।\nशमे प्रयतमानस्य मम शासनकाङ्क्षिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Peace is good for you and for the Pandavas, who also long for your command, as I strive for it."}},{"n":16,"text":"स्वयं निष्कलमालक्ष्य संविधत्स्व विशां पते ।\nसहभूतास्तु भरतास्तवैव स्युर्जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your own side without fruit, make your arrangement, lord; if the Bharatas stay united, they will be yours alone, lord of men."}},{"n":17,"text":"धर्मार्थयोस्तिष्ठ राजन्पाण्डवैरभिरक्षितः ।\nन हि शक्यास्तथाभूता यत्नादपि नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, stay on the path of dharma and profit, guarded by the Pandavas; for no others, though they try, could be such protectors."}},{"n":18,"text":"न हि त्वां पाण्डवैर्जेतुं रक्ष्यमाणं महात्मभिः ।\nइन्द्रोऽपि देवैः सहितः प्रसहेत कुतो नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even Indra with the gods could overcome you when guarded by the great-souled Pandavas, so how could other kings?"}},{"n":19,"text":"यत्र भीष्मश्च द्रोणश्च कृपः कर्णो विविंशतिः ।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सोमदत्तोऽथ बाह्लिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Karna, Vivimshati, Ashvatthama, Vikarna, Somadatta and Bahlika,"}},{"n":20,"text":"सैन्धवश्च कलिङ्गश्च काम्बोजश्च सुदक्षिणः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरो भीमसेनः सव्यसाची यमौ तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saindhava, Kalinga, Kamboja, Sudakshina, and with Yudhishthira, Bhimasena, Savyasachin and the twins,"}},{"n":21,"text":"सात्यकिश्च महातेजा युयुत्सुश्च महारथः ।\nको नु तान्विपरीतात्मा युध्येत भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"the greatly splendid Satyaki and the great chariot-warrior Yuyutsu: what man of perverse mind would fight them, bull of the Bharatas?"}},{"n":22,"text":"लोकस्येश्वरतां भूयः शत्रुभिश्चाप्रधृष्यताम् ।\nप्राप्स्यसि त्वममित्रघ्न सहितः कुरुपाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you join with the Kurus and Pandavas, destroyer of foes, you will gain lordship of the world and be unassailable by enemies."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्य ते पृथिवीपालास्त्वत्समाः पृथिवीपते ।\nश्रेयांसश्चैव राजानः संधास्यन्ते परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rulers of the earth who are your equals and even better will make peace with you, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":24,"text":"स त्वं पुत्रैश्च पौत्रैश्च भ्रातृभिः पितृभिस्तथा ।\nसुहृद्भिः सर्वतो गुप्तः सुखं शक्ष्यसि जीवितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guarded on all sides by sons, grandsons, brothers, fathers and friends, you will be able to live in happiness."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतानेव पुरोधाय सत्कृत्य च यथा पुरा ।\nअखिलां भोक्ष्यसे सर्वां पृथिवीं पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keeping these before you and honoring them as before, you will enjoy the entire earth, lord of the earth."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतैर्हि सहितः सर्वैः पाण्डवैः स्वैश्च भारत ।\nअन्यान्विजेष्यसे शत्रूनेष स्वार्थस्तवाखिलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with all these Pandavas and your own, Bharata, you will conquer other enemies; all this is to your own advantage."}},{"n":27,"text":"तैरेवोपार्जितां भूमिं भोक्ष्यसे च परंतप ।\nयदि संपत्स्यसे पुत्रैः सहामात्यैर्नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will enjoy the land won by them, scorcher of foes, if you agree with your sons and ministers, lord of men."}},{"n":28,"text":"संयुगे वै महाराज दृश्यते सुमहान्क्षयः ।\nक्षये चोभयतो राजन्कं धर्ममनुपश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great destruction is seen in war, great king; and when both sides are destroyed, what dharma do you see?"}},{"n":29,"text":"पाण्डवैर्निहतैः संख्ये पुत्रैर्वापि महाबलैः ।\nयद्विन्देथाः सुखं राजंस्तद्ब्रूहि भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me, bull of the Bharatas, what happiness you would find if the Pandavas or your mighty sons were killed in battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"शूराश्च हि कृतास्त्राश्च सर्वे युद्धाभिकाङ्क्षिणः ।\nपाण्डवास्तावकाश्चैव तान्रक्ष महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandavas and your people are all brave, skilled in weapons and eager for war; protect them from a great fear."}},{"n":31,"text":"न पश्येम कुरून्सर्वान्पाण्डवांश्चैव संयुगे ।\nक्षीणानुभयतः शूरान्रथेभ्यो रथिभिर्हतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let us not see all the Kurus and Pandavas worn down in battle, heroes struck from their chariots by chariot-fighters on both sides."}},{"n":32,"text":"समवेताः पृथिव्यां हि राजानो राजसत्तम ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्ना नाशयेयुरिमाः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, the kings gathered on earth, overcome by wrath, may destroy these people."}},{"n":33,"text":"त्राहि राजन्निमं लोकं न नश्येयुरिमाः प्रजाः ।\nत्वयि प्रकृतिमापन्ने शेषं स्यात्कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, save this world, so that these people do not perish; if you return to your true nature, Kuru's delight, something will remain."}},{"n":34,"text":"शुक्ला वदान्या ह्रीमन्त आर्याः पुण्याभिजातयः ।\nअन्योन्यसचिवा राजंस्तान्पाहि महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pure, generous, modest, noble, of holy birth, helping one another, king: protect them from great fear."}},{"n":35,"text":"शिवेनेमे भूमिपालाः समागम्य परस्परम् ।\nसह भुक्त्वा च पीत्वा च प्रतियान्तु यथागृहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let these rulers of the earth meet one another in peace, eat and drink together, and go home each to his own house,"}},{"n":36,"text":"सुवाससः स्रग्विणश्च सत्कृत्य भरतर्षभ ।\nअमर्षांश्च निराकृत्य वैराणि च परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"well dressed and garlanded, honored, bull of the Bharatas, having dispelled anger and enmities, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":37,"text":"हार्दं यत्पाण्डवेष्वासीत्प्राप्तेऽस्मिन्नायुषः क्षये ।\nतदेव ते भवत्वद्य शश्वच्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The affection you had toward the Pandavas, now that the time of your life is near its end, let it be yours today and always, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":38,"text":"बाला विहीनाः पित्रा ते त्वयैव परिवर्धिताः ।\nतान्पालय यथान्यायं पुत्रांश्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were children deprived of their father and raised by you; protect them and your own sons as is just, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":39,"text":"भवतैव हि रक्ष्यास्ते व्यसनेषु विशेषतः ।\nमा ते धर्मस्तथैवार्थो नश्येत भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"You must protect them especially in times of misfortune; let your dharma and your wealth not be lost, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":40,"text":"आहुस्त्वां पाण्डवा राजन्नभिवाद्य प्रसाद्य च ।\nभवतः शासनाद्दुःखमनुभूतं सहानुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, bowing and propitiating you, say: at your command we with our followers have borne suffering."}},{"n":41,"text":"द्वादशेमानि वर्षाणि वने निर्व्युषितानि नः ।\nत्रयोदशं तथाज्ञातैः सजने परिवत्सरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These twelve years we spent in the forest, and the thirteenth, unknown, a year among people."}},{"n":42,"text":"स्थाता नः समये तस्मिन्पितेति कृतनिश्चयाः ।\nनाहास्म समयं तात तच्च नो ब्राह्मणा विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resolved that you, our father, would stand by us in that compact, we did not break the agreement, as the brahmanas know."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्मिन्नः समये तिष्ठ स्थितानां भरतर्षभ ।\nनित्यं संक्लेशिता राजन्स्वराज्यांशं लभेमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, keep to that compact for us who kept it; always tormented, king, let us get a share of our own kingdom."}},{"n":44,"text":"त्वं धर्ममर्थं युञ्जानः सम्यङ्नस्त्रातुमर्हसि ।\nगुरुत्वं भवति प्रेक्ष्य बहून्क्लेशांस्तितिक्ष्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, joining dharma and profit, ought rightly to save us; seeing your seniority, we bear many hardships."}},{"n":45,"text":"स भवान्मातृपितृवदस्मासु प्रतिपद्यताम् ।\nगुरोर्गरीयसी वृत्तिर्या च शिष्यस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So treat us like a mother and father; Bharata, the conduct of a teacher toward a pupil is weightier than a teacher's own."}},{"n":46,"text":"पित्रा स्थापयितव्या हि वयमुत्पथमास्थिताः ।\nसंस्थापय पथिष्वस्मांस्तिष्ठ राजन्स्ववर्त्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A father should set right us who have gone astray; set us on the paths, king, and stand yourself on your own road."}},{"n":47,"text":"आहुश्चेमां परिषदं पुत्रास्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nधर्मज्ञेषु सभासत्सु नेह युक्तमसांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons, bull of the Bharatas, say of this assembly: it is not fitting or proper where the members know dharma."}},{"n":48,"text":"यत्र धर्मो ह्यधर्मेण सत्यं यत्रानृतेन च ।\nहन्यते प्रेक्षमाणानां हतास्तत्र सभासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where dharma is slain by adharma and truth by falsehood while the members look on, the members are slain."}},{"n":49,"text":"विद्धो धर्मो ह्यधर्मेण सभां यत्र प्रपद्यते ।\nन चास्य शल्यं कृन्तन्ति विद्धास्तत्र सभासदः ।\nधर्म एतानारुजति यथा नद्यनुकूलजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where dharma, pierced by adharma, enters an assembly and its members do not draw out the dart, they themselves are pierced; dharma strikes them as a river destroys trees on its bank."}},{"n":50,"text":"ये धर्ममनुपश्यन्तस्तूष्णीं ध्यायन्त आसते ।\nते सत्यमाहुर्धर्मं च न्याय्यं च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who see dharma and yet sit silent, brooding, bull of the Bharatas, speak the truth, dharma and what is right, in effect."}},{"n":51,"text":"शक्यं किमन्यद्वक्तुं ते दानादन्यज्जनेश्वर ।\nब्रुवन्तु वा महीपालाः सभायां ये समासते ।\nधर्मार्थौ संप्रधार्यैव यदि सत्यं ब्रवीम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What else can I say to you, lord of men, except of giving? Or let the kings sitting in the assembly speak, after weighing dharma and profit, if what I say is true."}},{"n":52,"text":"प्रमुञ्चेमान्मृत्युपाशात्क्षत्रियान्क्षत्रियर्षभ ।\nप्रशाम्य भरतश्रेष्ठ मा मन्युवशमन्वगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Release these kshatriyas from the noose of death, bull of kshatriyas; calm yourself, best of the Bharatas, and do not fall under anger's sway."}},{"n":53,"text":"पित्र्यं तेभ्यः प्रदायांशं पाण्डवेभ्यो यथोचितम् ।\nततः सपुत्रः सिद्धार्थो भुङ्क्ष्व भोगान्परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give the Pandavas the share of their father's estate as is due; then, with your sons, your aim accomplished, enjoy pleasures, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":54,"text":"अजातशत्रुं जानीषे स्थितं धर्मे सतां सदा ।\nसपुत्रे त्वयि वृत्तिं च वर्तते यां नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know Ajatashatru always stands in dharma with the good, and what conduct he maintains toward you and your sons, lord of men."}},{"n":55,"text":"दाहितश्च निरस्तश्च त्वामेवोपाश्रितः पुनः ।\nइन्द्रप्रस्थं त्वयैवासौ सपुत्रेण विवासितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burned and cast out, he still sought refuge in you; and by you with your sons he was banished from Indraprastha."}},{"n":56,"text":"स तत्र निवसन्सर्वान्वशमानीय पार्थिवान् ।\nत्वन्मुखानकरोद्राजन्न च त्वामत्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, bringing all the kings under his sway, he made them look to you as their leader, and never transgressed you."}},{"n":57,"text":"तस्यैवं वर्तमानस्य सौबलेन जिहीर्षता ।\nराष्ट्राणि धनधान्यं च प्रयुक्तः परमोपधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he so conducted himself, Saubala, wishing to seize his kingdoms, wealth and grain, used a supreme trick on him."}},{"n":58,"text":"स तामवस्थां संप्राप्य कृष्णां प्रेक्ष्य सभागताम् ।\nक्षत्रधर्मादमेयात्मा नाकम्पत युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, of immeasurable soul, though he reached that state and saw Krishna brought into the assembly, did not waver from his kshatriya dharma."}},{"n":59,"text":"अहं तु तव तेषां च श्रेय इच्छामि भारत ।\nधर्मादर्थात्सुखाच्चैव मा राजन्नीनशः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I, Bharata, wish the good of you and of them; king, do not destroy the people of dharma, profit and happiness."}},{"n":60,"text":"अनर्थमर्थं मन्वाना अर्थं वानर्थमात्मनः ।\nलोभेऽतिप्रसृतान्पुत्रान्निगृह्णीष्व विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Restrain your sons, who mistake harm for gain and gain for harm and are given over to greed, lord of the people."}},{"n":61,"text":"स्थिताः शुश्रूषितुं पार्थाः स्थिता योद्धुमरिंदमाः ।\nयत्ते पथ्यतमं राजंस्तस्मिंस्तिष्ठ परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Parthas, subduers of foes, stand ready to serve you, and ready to fight; stand upon what is most beneficial for you, king."}},{"n":62,"text":"तद्वाक्यं पार्थिवाः सर्वे हृदयैः समपूजयन् ।\nन तत्र कश्चिद्वक्तुं हि वाचं प्राक्रामदग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings in their hearts honored those words, but no one there ventured to speak first."}}]}]}